            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.137,
            0.849,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, in an expression having two terms, swapping them does not change the value."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.18,
            0.741,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.259,
                0.18,
                0.741,
                0.223
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.232,
            0.848,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now consider an expression having three terms: (–7) + 10 + (–11). Let us add these terms in the following two different orders:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.277,
            0.644,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.355,
                0.277,
                0.644,
                0.34
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.349,
            0.826,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(adding the first two terms and then adding their sum to the third term)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.395,
            0.642,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.356,
                0.395,
                0.642,
                0.458
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.469,
            0.819,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(adding the last two terms and then adding their sum to the first term)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.506,
            0.724,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you see? The sums are the same in both cases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.523,
            0.847,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Again, we know that while adding positive numbers, grouping them in any of the above two ways gives the same sum."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.571,
            0.847,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Will this also hold when there are terms having negative numbers as well? Take some more expressions and check."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.619,
            0.794,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you explain why this is happening using the Token Model of integers that we saw in the Class 6 textbook of mathematics?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.828,
            0.608,
            0.928,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.828,
                0.608,
                0.928,
                0.664
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.668,
            0.848,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, grouping the terms of an expression in either of the following ways gives the same value.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.715,
            0.846,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.152,
                0.715,
                0.846,
                0.763
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.774,
            0.848,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider the expression (–7) + 10 + (–11) again. What happens when we change the order and add –7 and –11 first, and then add this sum to 10? Will we get the same sum as before?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.829,
            0.848,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that adding the terms of the expression (–7) + 10 + (–11) in any order gives the same sum of –8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 19,
